# Line endings for the bytes that leave this repository (DECISIONS.md D-0035,
# row D9).
#
# `files` packs `src/` beside `dist/`, so the sources in a tarball are whatever
# the packer's checkout holds. Without an attribute, a clone under
# `core.autocrlf=true` writes CRLF `.ts` files and packs different bytes than a
# Linux clone does, with no compiler involved at all. `eol=lf` makes the working
# tree LF on every platform, so a rebuilt tarball is the same tarball.
#
# `dist/` is gitignored today and the rule is therefore inert for it; it is
# written because the emitted tree is the other half of the same question, and a
# route that ever tracks build output must not have to remember this.
src/** text eol=lf
dist/** text eol=lf
